==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
Lizalfos Horns are winding [[Monster Horn]]s dropped by all varieties of [[Lizalfos]] as well as [[Stalizalfos]] when defeated. They are too hard to [[Cooking|Cook]] [[Food]] with, but they can be used in a [[Cooking Pot]] with critters to make [[Elixir]]s with an additional minute and 10 seconds to their duration.<ref name="BotW Inventory"/> The [[Kochi Dye Shop]] also accepts Lizalfos Horns as an ingredient for Gray [[Dye]]. Finally, [[Kilton]] at the [[Fang and Bone]] will take Lizalfos Horns in exchange for [[Mon]].

Three Lizalfos Horns are used to upgrade each piece of the [[Zora Set]] to its first tier at a [[Great Fairy Fountain]].
{{Material Armors|BotW|Lizalfos Horn}}

==={{TotK|-}}===
{{Compendium/Extract/TotK|Lizalfos Horn}}
Lizalfos Horns are sharp, knife-like [[Monster Horn]]s dropped by standard [[Lizalfos]] and [[Stalizalfos]]. They can [[Cooking|Cooked]] with critters to brew [[Elixir]]s with an additional 40 seconds added to their duration.<ref name="TotK Inventory"/> They grant an additional 8 attack power when [[Fuse]]d with [[Weapon]]s and [[Arrow]]s.

Lizalfos Horns are required to upgrade the following pieces of [[Armor]] at a [[Great Fairy Fountain]]:
{{Material Armors|TotK|Lizalfos Horn}}

